// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every code the mental wellness (rehabilitation) templates and their
// extraction maps use, in one system. The 22 questionnaires in
// input/mental-health-templates carry their answer options on it, and the
// extraction StructureMaps stamp its codes onto everything they create, so a
// consumer needs exactly one CodeSystem to read what the forms produce.
//
// Three kinds of concept live here, and the comment banners mark them out:
// instrument and document types the maps assert; answer options the forms
// offer; and question or clause codes, whose code is the question item's own
// linkId (or its suffix after the first dot where the map says so), so adding
// a question to a template carries its concept through without editing a map.
//
// Generated from the templates; regenerate rather than hand-edit when a
// template changes (scripts live with the assessment work).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CodeSystem: MentalWellnessCodeSystem
Id: mental-wellness-codesystem
Title: "Mental Wellness Code System"
Description: "A single code system for the mental wellness and rehabilitation templates: the instruments and document types their extractions assert, the answer options the forms offer, and the question and clause concepts their answers hang off. One system rather than two dozen invented ones, so every extracted resource is readable against one published vocabulary."
* ^status = #active
* ^experimental = false
* ^caseSensitive = true
* ^content = #complete

// ── Assessment instruments and clinical record types ──
* #stage-of-change "Stage of change"
* #general-physical-examination "General physical examination"
* #clinical-history "Clinical history"
* #mental-state-examination "Mental state examination"
* #clinical-formulation "Clinical formulation"
* #bdi "Beck's Depression Inventory"
* #chemical-use-history "Chemical use history"

// ── Assessment domains (shared by the ASI and the SOAP problem areas) ──
* #general-information "General information"
* #medical "Medical status"
* #employment "Employment and support status"
* #alcohol-drug "Alcohol and drug use"
* #legal "Legal status"
* #family-social "Family and social relationships"
* #psychiatric "Psychiatric status"

// ── Clinical risk flags ──
* #suicidal-thoughts-reported "Serious thoughts of suicide reported"
* #suicide-attempt-reported "Suicide attempt reported"
* #suicidal-thoughts-observed "Suicidal thoughts observed at interview"
* #suicidal-ideation-reported "Suicidal ideation reported"

